  "description": "A partial page: four records, then DFHRESP(ENDFILE) inside the loop rather than on the look-ahead, so a different arm runs. :1233-1237 ends the loop, sets CA-NEXT-PAGE-NOT-EXISTS and stores the key of the last record actually returned, because CARD-RECORD still holds it - an ENDFILE read returns no record and overwrites nothing. :1238-1240 moves 'NO MORE RECORDS TO SHOW'. The empty-result branch at :1241-1245 does not fire, because WS-SCRN-COUNTER is four. Rows five through seven keep the LOW-VALUES that MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-ALL-ROWS left at :1124, so 1200-SCREEN-ARRAY-INIT skips them at :716, :726 and :735 and all fifteen of their map items stay LOW-VALUES - including CRDSELnO, which is why a blank row and an unselected row are distinguishable on the wire.",
